# Openstage

> Openstage keeps a public page for each project a builder makes, kept current from GitHub: what they built and when, who visits the project's website, and what it earns. Builders claim a stage at openstage.dev/their-username, with a page per project.

Openstage is for indie and side-project builders. It reads a builder's public GitHub commits and gives each project a page of its own, from its first commit to today, with the milestones and launches the builder logs by hand. A project can also count the visits to its own website, through one script tag that sets no cookie, and show its MRR and paying customers from Stripe, through a read-only key. It is free to start. Openstage Pro is $7/month and adds every project's site visits, MRR on project pages, full analytics, the subscriber list and private entries. Openstage never posts on a user's behalf, and there are no likes or comments: it is a record, not a social network.

