## How it works
- Sign in with GitHub and claim a username. Anyone can preview the stage of a GitHub username first, with no sign-in.
- Public repos sync every 2 hours. Each project gets a page at openstage.dev/username/repo, with a chart of its commits and what shipped marked on it.
- Add milestones, launches and notes by hand, in one line.
- Count visits to a project's website with one script tag (no cookie), and show MRR and paying customers from Stripe with a read-only key. The builder picks which numbers visitors see. Openstage never ranks or rewrites what a builder wrote.
- Share one link at openstage.dev/your-username, with a social preview card, an embeddable badge and an RSS feed. Visitors can follow a builder or one project by email; the builder owns that list.

